# opcode	semantic class; no unsupported opcode silently completes
# This table is interpreter dispatch, not a full-domain numerical certificate.
# The bounded replay gate is QSA convert/attend and sym NT4 gate_up/down.
# A row means the interpreter has a model for the name; the model itself refuses every unmeasured modifier or
# architecture at execution. Rows with an architecture-limited model: v_wmma_f32_16x16x16_bf16 (gfx1201 measured;
# gfx1151 historical corpus only, fresh receipt pending), v_dot2_f32_f16/bf16 (gfx1201 only), and the gfx1201-only
# SWMMAC rows v_swmmac_f32_16x16x32_f16/bf16 and v_swmmac_i32_16x16x32_iu8/iu4/x64_iu4 (index_key 0/1, measured
# neg_lo/neg_hi, integer two-half CLAMP; accumulator NEG[2], float CLAMP and other OPSEL bits refused). The six
# rows v_swmmac_f16_16x16x32_f16, v_swmmac_bf16_16x16x32_bf16 and v_swmmac_f32_16x16x32_{fp8,bf8}_{fp8,bf8} execute
# ONLY in an exact domain (finite normal/zero inputs, |C|+sum|products| <= 2^P q, P = 24/11/8; no rounding,
# NaN, infinity or denormal model) and hard-error on everything else.
# s_setprio is an ISA-defined scheduling hint (wave priority; no architectural state), a no-op like s_nop.
# The AMDGPU unsigned-division expansion of the builder GEMM prologues (s_cvt_f32_u32, v_s_rcp_f32, s_mul_f32,
# s_cvt_u32_f32) executes on gfx1201 only, for denominators 1..=2^24 (hardware-measured stage by stage); v_div_scale_f32
# follows the measured exponent-field chain of emu/alu.rs. See float_edges.md.
# NO row, so a decoded program hard-errors at load: v_wmma_bf16_16x16x16_bf16 and every FP8/BF8 WMMA.
# v_maxmin_num_f32 (gfx1201 only, no source modifiers/omod/clamp) is the num_select composition, hardware-compared
# over every triple of a 48-value f32 set (float_edges.md, receipt gfx1201-maxmin-r1).
# See isa/emu/float_edges.md "Opcode-fill qualification (pending)".
# v_log_f32_e32, v_rsq_f32_e32 and v_sqrt_f32_e32 are outside that gate;
# their candidate numeric paths remain unqualified for the full input domain.
